WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.640
Look for evidence that vital-organ perfusion is failing: new confusion, syncope, weak pulses, cool clammy skin, falling pressure or significant respiratory distress. A rhythm name and a single pressure value cannot summarize stability. Establish what changed from the patient’s baseline.
应寻找重要器官灌注失败证据：新发意识模糊、晕厥、弱脉、皮肤冷湿、血压下降或显著呼吸困难。节律名称及一次血压不能概括稳定性，须明确相对患者基线改变了什么。

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:40.464
The school lists systolic pressure below ninety as a warning reference. Other pathways use different numbers for specific decisions. Do not wait for any cutoff if the patient is clearly deteriorating; likewise, a currently acceptable pressure does not erase new altered mentation or ischemic symptoms.
学校把收缩压低于90列为警示参考，其他流程在特定决策中可能使用不同数值。明显恶化时不能等界值才行动；当前血压尚可，也不能抹去新发意识变化或缺血症状。

00:00:40.464 --> 00:01:00.432
Assess the pattern rather than one sign. Sweating may have several causes, capillary refill is affected by temperature, and urine output is rarely measurable immediately in the field. When available, reduced urine output and delayed refill add context; neither should replace repeated clinical assessment.
应评估组合，而非单个征象。出汗原因很多，毛细血管再充盈受温度影响，现场通常也无法立即测尿量。可获得时，尿量减少及再充盈延迟可提供背景，但均不能取代反复临床评估。

00:01:00.432 --> 00:01:19.872
Repeat observations and relate them to symptoms, movement and interventions. A worsening trend or a mismatch between patient and monitor should increase concern. Communicate what you actually measured and what was reported historically rather than presenting all signs as direct measurements.
应重复观察，并联系症状、搬动和干预。恶化趋势或患者与监护不一致时，应提高警惕。交接须区分实际测量与历史描述，不能把所有征象都说成直接测得。

00:01:19.872 --> 00:01:41.928
Maintain suspicion when symptoms include unexplained dyspnoea, nausea, sweating, unusual fatigue or discomfort in the jaw, back or arm. Older adults and people with diabetes may have less prominent pain. These findings have several possible causes, so assess rather than automatically diagnosing ACS.
对原因不明的呼吸困难、恶心、出汗、异常疲乏或下颌、背部、手臂不适，应保持警惕。老年人及糖尿病患者疼痛可能不突出，但这些表现也有多种原因，因此应评估，而不是自动诊断 ACS。

00:01:41.928 --> 00:02:00.048
The school calls these atypical presentations. Do not turn that label into a sex-based stereotype: women also commonly have chest pain, and people outside the named groups can have pain-free ACS. Use interpreters and careful questions when communication barriers affect the history.
学校把这些称为非典型表现，但不能变成性别刻板印象：女性也常有胸痛，其他人群也可能无痛 ACS。若沟通障碍影响病史，应使用口译和细致询问。

00:02:00.048 --> 00:02:20.736
For suspected ACS, the linked twenty twenty-five guideline recommends acquisition and interpretation of a twelve-lead ECG within ten minutes of first medical contact. Work efficiently without sacrificing quality, and do not misapply that timing as a reason to postpone immediate resuscitation.
针对疑似 ACS，所链接的2025指南建议首次医疗接触后10分钟内采集并判读十二导联。应兼顾效率和质量，不能把这个时限当作推迟立即复苏的理由。

00:02:20.736 --> 00:02:40.656
If the first ECG is nondiagnostic but symptoms persist, clinical suspicion remains high or the patient worsens, repeated ECG assessment can reveal change. A normal monitoring lead is not equivalent to a normal diagnostic twelve-lead, and neither independently excludes ACS.
若首份记录无诊断性，但症状持续、临床高度怀疑或患者恶化，重复心电评估可能发现变化。监护导联正常不等于诊断性十二导联正常，二者也都不能独立排除 ACS。

00:02:40.656 --> 00:03:01.992
The school lesson specifies a three-minute pre-notification target after a qualifying high-risk ECG finding. Retain it as the school’s performance expectation for practice. The reviewed guideline supports prompt system activation, but this lesson does not verify the school’s exact three-minute wording as a universal guideline rule.
学校课文规定，在符合条件的高危心电发现后以3分钟内预警为目标；练习时保留这一学校表现要求。所核对指南支持迅速启动系统，但本课未证实学校的具体3分钟文字是普遍指南条款。

00:03:01.992 --> 00:03:24.864
Class one describes recommendation strength, not automatically the highest evidence level. Follow the actual receiving pathway and medical direction for destination and activation. The school mentions advanced twelve-lead patterns as a bridge to ECG 301; do not invent their detailed diagnostic criteria in ECG 101.
I 类描述推荐强度，不自动等于最高证据等级。目的地与启动须遵循实际接收流程及医疗指导。学校提及高级十二导联形态是向 ECG 301 过渡，不应在 ECG 101 编造其详细诊断标准。

00:03:24.864 --> 00:03:47.184
An unstable patient with a nonspecific ECG still needs urgent assessment and authorized support. ACS may be one possibility, but bleeding, sepsis, pulmonary embolism and other causes can produce similar deterioration. Do not let the school examples narrow every shock presentation to coronary disease.
不稳定患者即使心电图不特异，也需要紧急评估及授权支持。ACS 可能是原因之一，但出血、脓毒症、肺栓塞等也可类似恶化，不能让学校例子把所有休克都缩窄为冠脉病。

00:03:47.184 --> 00:04:09.720
For possible ACS, combine symptom history, serial physiology, diagnostic ECG and changes over time. Communicate suspected risk and limitations early. Oxygen, medicines and other interventions follow indications and the local pathway, not a blanket instruction based solely on an ECG label.
对可能 ACS，应结合症状病史、连续生理评估、诊断性心电图及时间变化，尽早报告风险和局限。氧疗、药物等干预须符合适应证及本地流程，不能仅凭心电标签一律实施。
